  "instance_name": "karen_stereotype",
  "label": "Karen Stereotype",
  "description": "A derogatory stereotype referring to a woman (often white, middle-class, or upper-middle-class) perceived as entitled, aggressive, or unreasonable, particularly in public or service settings. The term is used pejoratively to describe individuals who are seen as demanding, confrontational, or overly assertive — often in ways that are considered disruptive or unreasonable. The stereotype is rooted in misogynistic and classist assumptions about women who are perceived as overly emotional or entitled.",
